  "implementation_notes": [
    "Finite population correction in Wilson intervals: the sample size is replaced by the effective size n(N-1)/(N-n); when the whole stratum is sampled (n = N) the interval collapses to the point estimate.",
    "Newcombe difference intervals use the hybrid score method on the corrected Wilson limits of the two strata.",
    "Bootstrap percentile intervals use linear interpolation between order statistics; a resample in which a run has no item in a stratum where it has edges is undefined for that run and is dropped; the number dropped is reported.",
    "H-E2 pooled proportion: each item weighs one; its value is the mean over its runs; the Wilson interval for the pooled value uses the number of items."
  ],
